 "provenance_html": "<p>Same generator and planted structure as the PID sweep (K = 16 latent factors, R/S/U = 0.1/0.3/0.6, two cross-modal interaction pairs at \u03bb = 10, 64 + 64 features), simulated at each cohort size with 10 seeds (Synthegra commit 0f0dadd). 3-fold stratified CV, held-out C-index.</p><p>Early linear = ridge Cox; early non-linear = boosted survival model (150 trees, depth 2); intermediate = the best of Synthegra's neural intermediate-fusion architectures (simple sum, temporal attention, cross-attention, GMU, grouped Kronecker) \u00d7 hidden size [16, 64] \u00d7 learning rate [0.001, 0.003], selected per cohort on the validation C-index and reported on the test folds. Best single layer = best of the two layers alone (boosted model or unimodal neural net). IBS = integrated Brier score over 100 time points across the test fold's follow-up with Kaplan-Meier censoring weights (pycox EvalSurv), lower is better; for IBS the gain is best-single minus model, so positive is still better. Lines: mean gain over the best single layer; bands: 2.5\u201397.5 % across seeds.</p>"
